===Etymology 2===
Shortened from {{m|en|bebop}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|music genre}} A [[style]] of [[improvised]] [[jazz]] from the 1940s.
#* {{RQ:Kerouac On the Road|chapter=13|passage=That grand wild sound of '''bop''' floated from beer parlors; it mixed medleys with every kind of cowboy and boogie-woogie in the American night.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|countable}} A good [[song]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022-09-05|author=Maria Sherman|title=The essential Harry Styles song book|journal={{w|Rolling Stone|Rolling Stone UK}}|url=https://www.rollingstone.co.uk/music/lists/harry-styles-essential-songs-solo-one-direction-22241/|passage=In the later years of One Direction, especially those after the departure of Zayn Malik, the boy band morphed into the vintage pop-rock group of their (well, let’s be real, Harry’s) dreams. ‘What a Feeling’ feels prescient: its Fleetwood Mac style structure laid the groundwork for Styles’ future endeavours. It’s a '''bop'''!}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[casual]] [[party]] with [[dance|dancing]]; a [[disco]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Barbara Claypole White|title=The Unfinished Garden|page=308
|passage={{...}} their first kiss during the school '''bop''', with Paul Weller singing “You're the Best Thing” and everything tingling from her toes up {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|countable|Oxbridge slang}} A [[party]] hosted by a [[college]]'s [[JCR]] or [[MCR]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=Johnny Rich|title=Push Guide to Which University|page=472|passage=Theatres; Music House used for bands; May Ball; very popular weekly '''bops''' in JCR and MCR; library (57,000 books); 40 networked PCs, 24-hrs.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=Owen Jones|title=Chavs: The Demonization of the Working Class|page=120|passage=At universities like Oxford, middle-class students hold 'chav '''bops'''' where they dress up as this working-class caricature.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col-auto|en|bopper|boppish|boppy|postbop|hard bop|post-bop}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# To [[dance]] to [[music]] with a marked beat.
#: {{ux|en|She was '''bopping''' to the song's drum beats.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2019-02-17|work=Genius News|author=Chris Mench|url=https://genius.com/a/blueface-wants-people-to-pay-attention-to-his-lyrics-not-just-bop-to-his-music|title=Blueface Wants People To Pay Attention To His Lyrics, Not Just '''Bop''' To His Music|passage=I’d rather you be stiff with a stuck look on your face than just '''bopping''', not even listening to what a nigga saying.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=2020-10-08|title=Clothes|author=Tall Boy Special|url=https://genius.com/Tall-boy-special-clothes-lyrics|passage=The hat was sorta dancing, just '''bopping around'''<br/>Floating in the air six feet above the ground}}

===Etymology 3===
Variant of {{m|en|whop|t=to move around quickly with an impact}} and {{m|en|bob|t=to move gently vertically}} as well as from the dances above interpreted as a manner of locomotion.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|informal|ambitransitive}} To walk casually; to [[stroll]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=S. E. Finken|title=Near Misses|page=199
|passage="I '''bopped''' down to take Charlie out for a surprise lunch, but he's out at the warehouse doing something with somebody or something. So I'm letting you take me to lunch."}}
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist={{w|Aitch (rapper)|Aitch}}|title=w:Taste (Make It Shake)|date=31-07-2019|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nDuVsE6yGdAt=19|passage=I'm just '''bopping''', give a fuck who's in the place<p><small>In the music video around this line, he is walking on road and barely dancing.</small></p>}}
# {{lb|en|slang|ambitransitive}} To [[have sex]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:copulate}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Tim Cockey|title=The Hearse You Came In On|passage=I'm here because your wife and I have been '''bopping''' like bunnies. Here are the pictures to prove it.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Terrence Oral Taylor|title=Dancing with the Boogie Man|page=196|passage={{...}} You aren't the Boy Scout you pretend to be. I'll bet you two '''bopped''' all night long.” Colin shook his head. “You're wrong. We didn't.” “You just took her home?” “That's about it.”}}
# {{lb|en|slang|ambitransitive}} To [[fellate]].
#* {{quote-song|en|date=28-06-2016|lyricist=Loski|artist=w:Loski|title=Hazards|note=[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2hojXQcOVzg&t=159 2:39]|url=https://genius.com/Loski-hazards-lyrics|passage=[[squad|Squa']] said she just done the 6, now she on the ends just boppin' (Bad, she bad)<br/>Now she on the ends just '''boppin''' (Boppin')<p><small>The rapper's gestures do not leave room for ambiguity.</small></p>}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang|offensive}} A promiscuous woman, especially in the context of having a high [[body count]] or giving [[fellatio]] to many men.

